lines+=['','**The registered first-quartet-dominance prediction is falsified by native240.** In the other five cells, the original 85.699 quartet dominates and the new pair contributes only about1e-5 to4e-4 in magnitude. Native240 switches: the new 240.405 quartet contributes about−4.09807, while the first contributes only about−9.65e-6. The new pair lies inside its cutoff. This independently identifies a different negative-quartet mechanism on that selected vector; it is not a universal first-pair or multiplicity-only effect. Matched240 still selects a vector dominated by the first quartet. The contrast is conditional on the different complements and selected minimizers; it is not a common-vector operator comparison or a proof of eventual dominance.','','## Every quartet, with its actual complex evaluation','','|m|mode|height|belowT?|ReF|ImF|Weil quartet|metric correction|','|---:|---|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
